# Cursor Rules for NeuralCSSR Project

## Environment Management
ALWAYS use `uv` for package management and running Python scripts:
- Use `uv sync` to install dependencies
- Use `uv run python script.py` for all Python script execution
- Never use `pip` directly for this project
- Use `uv run --with torch --with numpy python script.py` when specific packages are needed

## Command Formatting
ALWAYS provide example commands in a format that can be directly copied and run:
- Use complete, executable command examples
- Include all necessary flags and parameters
- Show the exact terminal output format
- Use proper bash syntax with `#` for comments
- Ensure commands work from the project root directory unless otherwise specified

## Code Style
- Follow PEP 8 style guidelines for Python code
- Use descriptive variable names and function names
- Include docstrings for all public functions and classes
- Use type hints where appropriate
- Keep functions focused and single-purpose

## Documentation
- Update CURSOR.md when adding new machines or workflows
- Include usage examples for all new functions
- Document any breaking changes or new dependencies
- Keep command examples up-to-date and runnable

## Testing
- Include basic validation of generated datasets
- Verify model training achieves expected loss levels
- Check that discovery algorithms produce reasonable state counts
- Test new machines with the full pipeline before committing
